  "functions": [
    "FUNC.CUBERANKEDMEMBER"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "CUBERANKEDMEMBER accepts set expressions directly or via cell references, truncates rank (with logical/numeric-text coercion), and returns #VALUE! on invalid rank text before connection lookup",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, CUBERANKEDMEMBER(connection, set_expression, rank, [caption]) accepts either a CUBESET cell reference or an inline set expression string, reads rank by truncating numbers (1.9 -> 1), coercing logicals (TRUE -> 1) and numeric strings (\"1\" -> 1), rejects non-numeric rank text (\"hello\", \"1,234\") with #VALUE! before connection lookup, and returns #N/A for rank < 1 or exceeding the set size. All 4,287 full-bank CUBERANKEDMEMBER rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in DnaCalc crates/calc-host/tests/fixtures/cube/measured.xlsx (A104-A107), pivot_cube/oracle.xlsx (A131-A132), and CalcFunc-Evidence admit2-answers-cuberankedmember-scalar.json; 4,287/4,287 full-bank rows match.",
